id: pm-rust-6q0n
title: Remove personal author identity from public Git history
description: The existing public history contains a non-noreply personal-domain author identity and cannot pass the promised full-history privacy gate without a coordinated history rewrite.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 0
tags[3]: history,privacy,release
created_at: "2026-08-07T11:03:50.188Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T11:03:50.188Z"
assignee: maintainer
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Every commit and tag reachable from every public remote ref uses an approved public noreply or bot identity; A full raw-history secret scan and identity audit pass after the rewrite; Maintainer approval and downstream coordination are recorded before any force push
definition_of_ready: Maintainer explicitly approves destructive public-history replacement and the author mapping
value: Restores the package privacy promise
impact: Blocks publication and release readiness until resolved
outcome: Public history contains no personal-domain identity metadata
why_now: The required full-history audit detected this before the native create PR
parent: pm-rust-u4al
reviewer: maintainer
risk: critical
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-release-hardening
release: 0.1.0-alpha.2
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: Public Git repository full raw history
repro_steps: Enumerate author and committer identities for all refs and classify non-noreply domains
expected_result: Only approved public noreply and bot identities are reachable
actual_result: At least one existing reachable commit uses a personal-domain identity
affected_version: 0.1.0-alpha.1
component: release-governance
customer_impact: Personal identity metadata is already visible and package publication must remain disabled
body: "Do not publish a crate or tag a release until a maintainer approves a coordinated author-map rewrite and force-push plan. Preserve commit content and tags, notify consumers, rerun the full raw-history secret and identity audit, and verify every remote ref after replacement."
